@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title Claude in Chrome from a sandbox — the native host socket, carried across the boundary

' covers: internal/chromebridge/** (ScopeGate), defs/claudecode/mcp/proveo-lib/chrome-bridge.js, packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (proveo_chrome_bridge, _proveo_chrome_scope_ok), internal/run/choices.go, internal/egress/plan.go (HostBridge)

node "Operator's machine" as HOSTM <<host>> {
  component "Chrome + Claude in Chrome extension\n(the operator's logins, the extension's site permissions)" as CHROME <<cloud>>
  component "native messaging host\n""claude --chrome-native-host""" as NMH <<app>>
  database "LISTENS\n""/tmp/claude-mcp-browser-bridge-<user>/<pid>.sock""" as HSOCK <<db>>
  component "proveo run — ""internal/chromebridge""\nTCP relay, per-run token" as RELAY <<app>>
  component "picker add-on\n""chrome (host browser)"" — off by default" as PICK <<app>>
}

node "Agent container (docker backend)" as CONT <<host>> {
  component "chrome-bridge.js\n""proveo_chrome_bridge"" starts it before ""exec claude""" as CRELAY <<app>>
  database "LISTENS, same rule for <user>\n""/tmp/claude-mcp-browser-bridge-<user>/<pid>.sock""\n0700 dir · 0600 socket" as CSOCK <<db>>
  component "Claude Code ""--chrome""\nclaude-in-chrome MCP server (CONNECTS)" as CC <<app>>
}

component "sandbox VM (sbx)\nno route to the host" as SBX <<error>>
component "session with no accepted scope\n'Disabled: OAuth token has no scope…'" as SCOPE <<error>>
component "connection without the token\nclosed before a byte flows" as BAD <<error>>

CHROME ARROW_MAIN NMH : spawns, native messaging (stdio)
NMH    ARROW_MAIN HSOCK : creates, listens
CC     ARROW_MAIN CSOCK : newest ""*.sock"" in its dir
CSOCK  ARROW_MAIN CRELAY
CRELAY ARROW_MAIN RELAY : ""PROVEO_CHROME_BRIDGE=host.docker.internal:<port>""\nfirst line ""PROVEO-CHROME-BRIDGE <token>""
RELAY  ARROW_MAIN HSOCK : dials the newest socket,\npipes both ways
PICK   ARROW_MAIN RELAY : ticked → started for the run,\nenv + ""HostBridge"" on the egress plan
PICK   ARROW_ERROR SBX : greyed while docker (sandbox) is ticked —\nand on an sbx harness that box is now COMPULSORY,\nso ""PROVEO_SBX=0"" is the only way to reach this add-on
PICK   ARROW_ERROR SCOPE : greyed when the session's scopes\nname none of the three (""chromebridge.ScopeGate"")
RELAY  ARROW_ERROR BAD

note right of NMH
  **Who listens, who connects.** The native
  host is the server; Claude Code's MCP
  server is the client and picks the newest
  socket. Both halves of the bridge keep
  that shape, so neither Claude Code changes.
end note

note bottom of RELAY
  **TCP, because virtiofs drops sockets.** A
  bind mount cannot carry a Unix socket into
  Docker Desktop or OrbStack. The listener is
  loopback on macOS; the token is what guards
  Linux's bridge-facing address.
end note

note bottom of CRELAY
  **Same username rule as Claude Code.**
  ""os.userInfo().username"", else ""$USER"",
  ""$USERNAME"", ""default"". An arbitrary run-as
  uid lands on the fallback; guessing from
  the shell would miss the directory.
end note

note bottom of CC
  **--chrome is the only switch.**
  ""claudeInChromeDefaultEnabled"" is never
  persisted: the home outlives the run, and a
  later run would load browser tools that
  cannot connect. Onboarding IS marked seen.
end note

note right of SBX
  **Docker backend only.** Every outbound TCP
  of a sandbox is proxied on the host and the
  VM "cannot access your host network
  directly" (Docker Sandboxes security docs).
  Fallback prints why, never silently.
end note

note right of SCOPE
  **A rule about scopes, not variables.** The
  gate wants one of ""user:profile"",
  ""user:office"" or ""user:ccr_inference"", and it
  runs BEFORE ""--chrome"" and
  ""CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_CFC"" — neither overrides
  it. But ""/api/oauth/validate"" is only NAMED
  in the message: the scopes are synthesised
  on the client from where the credential came.

  ""CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN"" → whatever
  ""CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_SCOPES"" says, else the
  literal ""user:inference"" — which is what
  ""claude setup-token"" mints. File-descriptor
  delivery → a default carrying
  ""user:ccr_inference"". A ""/login"" store → its
  real scopes. Two of the three paths pass;
  Anthropic's own cloud launcher sets both env
  vars and gets Chrome.

  ""CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN"" SHADOWS the store.
  ""ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"" does not.
end note

note as SbxViewport #F4F9FB
  **The sandbox backend takes the other route.** This bridge points OUTWARD: the
  agent reaches the operator's own Chrome through a relay on the host, named as
  ""host.docker.internal"" — which only the docker backend's bridge network
  resolves, and which a sandbox VM cannot name at all. sbx publishes ports the
  other way (host → sandbox), so it can never serve this direction.

  What it can serve is the mirror image: the agent's OWN Chromium, published to
  host loopback so the operator attaches DevTools or Playwright to it. That is
  the browser add-on's viewport — _spec/internal/sbx/browser-viewport.puml.
end note

@enduml
